# Cron Jobs & Scheduled Tasks

## Entry Point Pattern

```php
// reminders_cron.php — CLI only
define('ENVIRONMENT', 'production');
require_once __DIR__ . '/index.php';

log_message('info', '=== Cron Started: ' . date('Y-m-d H:i:s') . ' ===');
$CI = &get_instance();
$CI->load->model('Reminder_model');
// ... run tasks ...
log_message('info', '=== Cron Completed ===');
```

## Controller Guard

```php
public function __construct() {
    parent::__construct();
    if (!is_cli()) {
        show_404();
    }
}
```

## Reminder Processing

1. Fetch pending/upcoming records (with `is_deleted = 0`)
2. Bulk insert reminders via `insert_batch()` (max 500/batch)
3. Send pending in chunks (limit ~100/run)
4. Update status + retry count on failure (max 3 retries)

## Logging

```php
log_message('info', 'Cron: reminder_send | processed: 150 | sent: 145 | failed: 5');
log_message('error', 'Cron: reminder_send | error: email_service_down');
```

Include: cron_name, records processed, status. Never log sensitive content (full emails, message bodies).

## Windows Task Scheduler

Use `.ps1` or `.bat` scripts pointing to WAMP PHP 8.4:

```
C:\wamp64\bin\php\php8.4.0\php.exe reminders_cron_generate.php
```

## Best Practices

- Always `is_cli()` guard — prevent web access
- Batch operations, use transactions for multi-table changes
- Set explicit time limits (not `set_time_limit(0)`)
- Monitor last execution — alert if stale >24h
- Document schedule in PROJECT_MAP.md
